    <p>
      Derrick's single closest DNA match, at <strong>333.9 cM</strong>, is a
      <strong>Harrison</strong> in the United Kingdom, on the <em>paternal</em> side.
    </p>
    <p>
      Be careful with this. A woman marrying into a Figueiredo family is no blood relation of Ivone's,
      so this is not a link between the two surnames in any genetic sense. What it is: evidence that an
      English Harrison family was in Johannesburg in exactly these years, in the same
      Portuguese-Johannesburg world Ivone lived in — and Derrick's paternal cluster is English with a
      South African connection. Harrison is also a very common name.
      <span class="tag inf">Speculation, recorded so it is not lost</span>
    </p>
